# Six samples into a 3-deep reservoir and into an all_time accumulator. Powers
# of ten give every 3-subset a distinct sum under 10^6, exact in a double, so
# the reservoir's mean names which three it kept. The last pump reads the
# first five (the sixth is absorbed after the read, [LSER.8.6]): the all_time
# mean is Welford's over 1 to 10000, and the bag holds three of those five.
# @spec [LSMP.2.1] [LSER.16.3.3]
assert Gauge entity_id=g level=1.0
assert Sampler entity_id=s level=1.0
pump
assert Gauge entity_id=g level=10.0
assert Sampler entity_id=s level=10.0
pump
assert Gauge entity_id=g level=100.0
assert Sampler entity_id=s level=100.0
pump
assert Gauge entity_id=g level=1000.0
assert Sampler entity_id=s level=1000.0
pump
assert Gauge entity_id=g level=10000.0
assert Sampler entity_id=s level=10000.0
pump
assert Gauge entity_id=g level=100000.0
assert Sampler entity_id=s level=100000.0
pump
